Z||000000||Shianne||05-29-2001||08:32 PM||||Well I may be changing the engine.  I have a 2.5l 84 right now the engine is leaky and wore out.  I have heard and read about the 3.1l or 3.4l conversions.  Is this a praticle idea for an 84, and if so what kind of parts am I looking for do I have to find a different transmission, I have a 4 speed now.  <P>I realize I need to change the computer and do a bunch of rewiring.  Not so sure I want to do this~<P>Anyhow what is the best way to go I have also heard about a quad 4 conversion.  Is this simpler will it mount to my existing hardware IE transmission and mounts.<P>Thanks Pat<P>Pincher Creek AB<BR>Canada<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||tgowens||05-29-2001||09:18 PM||||the 3.4 is by far the easier of the swaps. You will need everything from the heads up from a 2.8 Fiero plus the wiring harness and ECM. The starter will need to be mounted on the opposite side of the 3.4 and in your case (since you have a 2.5) you will need to reroute the coolant line which runs to the back of the engine..........you can bolt up the same tranny but will need to modify one mount (for the A/C bracket.......much easier than the Quad Four.......||||reg||1
Z||000002||KRMFiero||05-29-2001||09:23 PM||||If you want to do a 3.1 or 3.4 it is basically the 2.8, why not just but a 2.8 Fiero? with the '84 there will be alot of stuff you have to move around/replace, you might as well do a Caddy or 3800 swap or sommthing. if you really want a 3.1 or 3.4 i would buy a 85+ with blown engine then go from there<P>Kyle<P>------------------<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (Red)<BR>1985 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (White)<P>     <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/~Physcokyle/sig2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Shianne||05-29-2001||11:30 PM||||I was not sure,  It is not possible to mount engine mounts on the existing subframe.  Also you say you need everything from the heads up?  This means intake and manifolds I assume.  <P>I am not sure which way to go, I was reading the other conversion swap on this site and was intrested in the 3800 possible too as I happen to have one in my garge it came out of an 86 buick lesaber.  Not sure if this is even worth the time though.  Other than that I guess I am stuck with putting another 2.5 in.  There are no motors that were simular in mounting or were a knock off of the 2.5??<P>Thanks for you input<P>Pat||||reg||1
